# Receiver environment. NAMES ONLY -- never commit values.
# Set these in the Vercel project's Environment Variables screen.

# REQUIRED. Shared secret the /api/paypal/ledger read endpoint demands as a
# bearer token. Without it the endpoint returns 503 and reads nothing.
# Set the SAME value in the environment of the machine that runs gate 5, so
# the gate can read the ledger. Never paste the value anywhere it is kept.
REHEARSAL_RECEIVER_TOKEN=

# REQUIRED. The durable arrival ledger. Without BOTH of these the webhook
# endpoint returns 503 rather than accepting a delivery it would then drop.
# PayPal retries a 503, so events are delayed, not lost.
#
# SUPABASE_URL is the project URL, https://<ref>.supabase.co. The receiver
# refuses any other host.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY is the project's secret key, shown as "secret key"
# (sb_secret_...) in current dashboards and "service_role" in older ones. It
# bypasses RLS, which is how the receiver writes to a table with RLS on and no
# policies. It is server-side only: it must never appear in a NEXT_PUBLIC_
# variable, in the repo, in a log, or in a local shell.
#
# The receiver sends it on the apikey header only. sb_secret_ keys are not JWTs,
# so the Authorization: Bearer transport may reject them. The variable name is
# kept for continuity; either key format works.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# OPTIONAL but recommended. With all three set, the receiver verifies every
# event's signature against PayPal and records verified true/false. Without
# them it records verified=null, which means "not attempted", not "failed".
PAYPAL_SELLER_CLIENT_ID=
PAYPAL_SELLER_CLIENT_SECRET=
REHEARSAL_WEBHOOK_ID=
